From eeca4cd711efc81413b8643c2ff4517b72f67893 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:08:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/27] Typer: experiments eqfilter, eqouter, eqclass (more
 equalities used by matching)

eqfilter: a closed pair may be coerced if the equality procedure proves it.
eqouter: when innermost mismatching parts cannot be coerced, the outermost
enclosing parts that can be are used.
eqclass: a part with unification variables is instantiated with the types of
its shape written in equalities, so that a generic given applies to a type
equal to an instance of its head.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011CH6tJP7hLkrpGFxEq7K6r
